# tinted-dircolors
# Scheme name: Windows High Contrast Light
# Scheme author: Fergus Collins (https://github.com/ferguscollins)
# Template author: tinted-dircolors (local), modelled on seebi/dircolors-solarized
#
# Portions Copyright (c) 2020 Sebastian Tramp, MIT License
# https://github.com/seebi/dircolors-solarized/blob/master/LICENSE
#
# Based on the GNU coreutils dircolors database (dircolors -p):
# Copyright (C) 1996-2025 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
# Copying and distribution of this file, with or without modification,
# are permitted provided the copyright notice and this notice are preserved.
#
# Colors are 24-bit truecolor (38;2;R;G;B / 48;2;R;G;B) taken from the scheme,
# so they do not depend on the terminal's 16/256-color palette.
#
# Usage: eval "$(dircolors -b this-file)"

# Terminals that get colors at all
COLORTERM ?*
TERM Eterm
TERM ansi
TERM *color*
TERM con[0-9]*x[0-9]*
TERM cons25
TERM console
TERM cygwin
TERM *direct*
TERM dtterm
TERM gnome
TERM hurd
TERM jfbterm
TERM konsole
TERM kterm
TERM linux
TERM linux-c
TERM mlterm
TERM putty
TERM rxvt*
TERM screen*
TERM st
TERM terminator
TERM tmux*
TERM vt100
TERM vt220
TERM xterm*

## Basic file attributes
RESET 0
NORMAL 00
FILE 00
DIR 01;38;2;0;0;128
LINK 38;2;0;128;128
MULTIHARDLINK 00
FIFO 38;2;128;128;0;48;2;232;232;232
SOCK 01;38;2;128;0;128
DOOR 01;38;2;128;0;128
BLK 01;38;2;128;128;0;48;2;232;232;232
CHR 01;38;2;128;128;0;48;2;232;232;232
ORPHAN 01;38;2;128;0;0;48;2;232;232;232
MISSING 01;38;2;128;0;0;48;2;232;232;232
SETUID 38;2;252;252;252;48;2;128;0;0
SETGID 38;2;252;252;252;48;2;128;128;0
CAPABILITY 38;2;128;0;0;48;2;232;232;232
STICKY_OTHER_WRITABLE 38;2;252;252;252;48;2;0;128;0
OTHER_WRITABLE 01;38;2;0;0;128;48;2;232;232;232
STICKY 38;2;252;252;252;48;2;0;0;128
EXEC 01;38;2;0;128;0

